 function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}+{90}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {720}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=n\\cdot {720}^{∘},$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-81523/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58c7cd44-30a9-5f61-822c-13640ad41c93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81523"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-29132"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=x+{45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate the zeros of \n\n$$\ny=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe zeros of this function are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x+{45}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x+{45}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘},$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection/774ddd8a004a03992aec8b69988c26d393b2b3d23d0a4a1a719a38e046741591" :answer/id #uuid "74d70cb0-a782-5ebe-885c-1247b0a8d9b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection/90c96fbe037c4fb273d63857e8c5e539fea154d4e96d956c702836bbdb448824" :answer/id #uuid "dfb6f450-2cf0-5bfc-8f47-283b9d1b10a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection/513f9fe6044a27d7e7c75e28e0903cb1a8f7514cae2f17d52773451e2a33062d" :answer/id #uuid "224f287c-b259-5a10-8504-65c84cb82ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection/358ce9a8d260d73895c414ca595e98671838692c3556ce5ee25b6965d7cd6172" :answer/id #uuid "a84e9581-d058-5f42-afac-c043baa18b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection/423052936de6df435b1750a4394f709b0e1b892997a5e96e6f1b876c065a41cc" :answer/id #uuid "d9d98f51-ae32-5572-aba0-6456829b11f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56b21d82-a2dd-5183-b87f-5dcdb4cabfbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117604/selection/90c96fbe037c4fb273d63857e8c5e539fea154d4e96d956c702836bbdb448824" :answer-field/choices ["q-117604/selection/774ddd8a004a03992aec8b69988c26d393b2b3d23d0a4a1a719a38e046741591" "q-117604/selection/90c96fbe037c4fb273d63857e8c5e539fea154d4e96d956c702836bbdb448824" "q-117604/selection/513f9fe6044a27d7e7c75e28e0903cb1a8f7514cae2f17d52773451e2a33062d" "q-117604/selection/358ce9a8d260d73895c414ca595e98671838692c3556ce5ee25b6965d7cd6172" "q-117604/selection/423052936de6df435b1750a4394f709b0e1b892997a5e96e6f1b876c065a41cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117604" :question/id #uuid "9c3e0f91-7a46-576f-bbc2-896556eab8e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-117604" :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the zeros of $y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate the zeros of \n\n$$\ny=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe zeros of this function are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117604/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58c7cd44-30a9-5f61-822c-13640ad41c93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117604"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection/9d7b241c595ae26afa57cf63b36061deb20e871bf325106d58e24914faab4b3b" :answer/id #uuid "faa20d5f-bfb5-5681-a8b6-22bfe73465af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={5}^{∘}-n\\cdot {30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection/c4cd9e504dbbe4bf716d191a0ad673d2c338788ecedd6090630d9a6597a55b74" :answer/id #uuid "2f0ccad4-d136-52e5-9477-264677827ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {60}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection/8e0bdc6dfed6d23213bad9932b43980050bdfb3a46368afa877613bbe6c30de4" :answer/id #uuid "efd7db13-cef9-5b7e-b572-6c7804177e8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-{5}^{∘}-n\\cdot {15}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection/3bc2625cf61ff81ce8a20ae60c8d2720ca637380349a9c80598b1cf26a879fc7" :answer/id #uuid "882258ab-ccca-513e-8ce5-e68723bbf084" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {30}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection/806092ba40a4482eb262179abf992f009ad872447c72368b08020f26f9fcd79b" :answer/id #uuid "c902d4a3-0b00-5508-b1ef-57588069cfd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {120}^{∘}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ef8916-928c-5bd7-8d9d-4d75d25bc03d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117598/selection/3bc2625cf61ff81ce8a20ae60c8d2720ca637380349a9c80598b1cf26a879fc7" :answer-field/choices ["q-117598/selection/9d7b241c595ae26afa57cf63b36061deb20e871bf325106d58e24914faab4b3b" "q-117598/selection/c4cd9e504dbbe4bf716d191a0ad673d2c338788ecedd6090630d9a6597a55b74" "q-117598/selection/8e0bdc6dfed6d23213bad9932b43980050bdfb3a46368afa877613bbe6c30de4" "q-117598/selection/3bc2625cf61ff81ce8a20ae60c8d2720ca637380349a9c80598b1cf26a879fc7" "q-117598/selection/806092ba40a4482eb262179abf992f009ad872447c72368b08020f26f9fcd79b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117598" :question/id #uuid "16284207-9647-5b5b-9f17-61612c3eaa5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-117598" :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the zeros of $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+{30}^{∘})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=6x+{30}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate the zeros of \n\n$$\ny=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe zeros of this function are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=n\\cdot {180}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 6x+{30}^{∘} & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & =-{30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {30}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=-{5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {30}^{∘},$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-117598/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58c7cd44-30a9-5f61-822c-13640ad41c93"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117598"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-236968"] :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=5x+{40}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the maxima of\n\n$$\ny=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe $X$-values at the maxima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the maxima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x+{40}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 5x & ={50}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={10}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that maximize $f(x)$ are given by $x={10}^{∘}+{72}^{∘}\\cdot n,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection/7d60a21a1b0831c7abf65803ac11ffc14b107623e9d33bbaf35fda906e12c7b0" :answer/id #uuid "08f4969f-f186-5624-bb00-4268fa7bb19d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection/fd0348a2137ddd9763b964bd8cefdc6109edff7383f398eee8b99c2c5916a365" :answer/id #uuid "689151fc-4192-5bf1-9f6b-f1b37f967130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection/513f9fe6044a27d7e7c75e28e0903cb1a8f7514cae2f17d52773451e2a33062d" :answer/id #uuid "24e23dc6-98fa-55f9-ac23-6c4a7be79742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection/5ee9e9df19832e25795624332baffcd0670184c7aa0152c4bec977c3e4bb2813" :answer/id #uuid "382f7488-3d43-5c5d-81b3-1061c716dd4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection/fa41bda4ab4549916b2d46f9b8df67fa341fdf3fb657ef7d7405d06ba7222066" :answer/id #uuid "8b43afcc-4a0e-5c0e-9787-53f8c603ca34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80e2806c-5c1a-5732-81c7-9677fcbf6ce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81532/selection/fd0348a2137ddd9763b964bd8cefdc6109edff7383f398eee8b99c2c5916a365" :answer-field/choices ["q-81532/selection/7d60a21a1b0831c7abf65803ac11ffc14b107623e9d33bbaf35fda906e12c7b0" "q-81532/selection/fd0348a2137ddd9763b964bd8cefdc6109edff7383f398eee8b99c2c5916a365" "q-81532/selection/513f9fe6044a27d7e7c75e28e0903cb1a8f7514cae2f17d52773451e2a33062d" "q-81532/selection/5ee9e9df19832e25795624332baffcd0670184c7aa0152c4bec977c3e4bb2813" "q-81532/selection/fa41bda4ab4549916b2d46f9b8df67fa341fdf3fb657ef7d7405d06ba7222066"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81532" :question/id #uuid "f2cccc79-47c0-5c44-8163-576242902ebf" :question/math-academy-id "q-81532" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the maxima of\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe $X$-values at the maxima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the maxima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 4x+\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{16}+n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that maximize $f(x)$ are given by $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}+n\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81532/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ff20d1-fa3d-50aa-90d1-7bcb848ee460"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81532"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection/b8d4d103913bf9d4df9ce0b9cd9b27cd4be59baeb236890bf50b08497b3c115e" :answer/id #uuid "cec76013-7f68-58f2-86ec-382734ec6f96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pi +2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection/1053fe744592bafe524d555eaa3b015a48e9aba9943334a4cdb69cf567a59982" :answer/id #uuid "48cfc92e-62ad-5337-99b7-96e0bdd1f4f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\pi +n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection/a94e83eae185bead966f30cf2e6b6f4796b2e36b3fb0c2157f6002a1c50cb94e" :answer/id #uuid "ebd754eb-9315-5231-a867-4f661ffb7ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection/41e674211a892b55342a0d47949d7ed837075bc96dfb3534cb9cbd65c69486cf" :answer/id #uuid "d76045c8-775e-5303-b9fb-cfe9528798ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3\\pi +6n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection/f8540115db7344f087691286bbea4eec4cfe817c01982c8cea82fdc4e6f96997" :answer/id #uuid "89ee4640-c59c-534d-bcfc-3ddc7aa8acd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+6n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc75f417-84f3-560b-84a0-ed98c8f94687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117612/selection/41e674211a892b55342a0d47949d7ed837075bc96dfb3534cb9cbd65c69486cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-117612/selection/b8d4d103913bf9d4df9ce0b9cd9b27cd4be59baeb236890bf50b08497b3c115e" "q-117612/selection/1053fe744592bafe524d555eaa3b015a48e9aba9943334a4cdb69cf567a59982" "q-117612/selection/a94e83eae185bead966f30cf2e6b6f4796b2e36b3fb0c2157f6002a1c50cb94e" "q-117612/selection/41e674211a892b55342a0d47949d7ed837075bc96dfb3534cb9cbd65c69486cf" "q-117612/selection/f8540115db7344f087691286bbea4eec4cfe817c01982c8cea82fdc4e6f96997"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117612" :question/id #uuid "fd0840cf-e777-54fd-b597-e33c20b593dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-117612" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the maxima of\n\n$$\ny=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe $X$-values at the maxima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the maxima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3} & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =3\\pi +6n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that maximize $f(x)$ are given by $x=3\\pi +6n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117612/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ff20d1-fa3d-50aa-90d1-7bcb848ee460"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117612"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection/4170f972a656533646dfcd7d02a96510be9eafc6b4188d5cba2058138b8bcf4e" :answer/id #uuid "add48800-8d0a-5927-94b8-0ff525f12cac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={60}^{∘}+{180}^{∘}\\cdot n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection/af264300655bcbddd69a5460db18da911a5057724c9f687896e538433d4fe8af" :answer/id #uuid "52bc6d51-9fa2-57e0-9b9d-6835a1828044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={60}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}\\cdot n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection/746d65d3d39e84c53ead0d7aa4c558bd7b8d1f5883faed5641f0d0289e7073b2" :answer/id #uuid "c106d17f-a8a2-53d5-b307-4eb9e68ff846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}\\cdot n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection/4a3ae138b9d22e40057c04328e9c456732ab2d168f8cb84e93f8b85b269003f8" :answer/id #uuid "8d7304e5-f521-5552-8513-7f902a40480c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={30}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}\\cdot n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection/7f9aeb39af171a23e024618d4e046fb8582a2d917e62d857443a2ba8f387b1df" :answer/id #uuid "2fb193ce-004b-5692-8439-80add257b89c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5cba708-098a-5548-ad8f-ab9c300b4a27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-236971/selection/4a3ae138b9d22e40057c04328e9c456732ab2d168f8cb84e93f8b85b269003f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-236971/selection/4170f972a656533646dfcd7d02a96510be9eafc6b4188d5cba2058138b8bcf4e" "q-236971/selection/af264300655bcbddd69a5460db18da911a5057724c9f687896e538433d4fe8af" "q-236971/selection/746d65d3d39e84c53ead0d7aa4c558bd7b8d1f5883faed5641f0d0289e7073b2" "q-236971/selection/4a3ae138b9d22e40057c04328e9c456732ab2d168f8cb84e93f8b85b269003f8" "q-236971/selection/7f9aeb39af171a23e024618d4e046fb8582a2d917e62d857443a2ba8f387b1df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-236971" :question/id #uuid "2110cd11-21af-58e7-b1f6-5968ca99c991" :question/math-academy-id "q-236971" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=3x.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the maxima of\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe $X$-values at the maxima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the maxima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ 3x & ={90}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\ x & ={30}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}\\cdot n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that maximize $f(x)$ are given by $x={30}^{∘}+{120}^{∘}\\cdot n,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-236971/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ff20d1-fa3d-50aa-90d1-7bcb848ee460"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-236971"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117613/selection/31026c8cd36f515d289ffbfef7def5f08f16b0a99a9036d87e0fe8681efe9a73" :answer/id #uuid "da2d6aec-b402-535f-937e-1578318cbb8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117613/selection