h expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the maxima of\n\n$$\ny=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe $X$-values at the maxima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the maxima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =2n\\pi  \\\\ 3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =2n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that maximize $f(x)$ are given by $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117613/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ff20d1-fa3d-50aa-90d1-7bcb848ee460"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117613"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection/64f4bdd26daf769cdf1888fb84a5697a3bec3a99a1ded94774a821635dd157ba" :answer/id #uuid "7e8deab8-df17-54d5-881a-4ec47fb15e48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+8n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection/bf9716302ce7c9f50805073e08d4170912d0e97c55ba14de9b2570374d0b53cb" :answer/id #uuid "4463e8d6-9464-520c-b63d-f4c4e42fe0c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+8n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection/4b55faefad2d0bf5e9b0f1e409536c4e172f1ff4106c57bacd0941fab6fd652d" :answer/id #uuid "cba79f61-cead-52e0-890c-2737a05615f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection/edcfd6d065adde0faa5b121e19e939fbfc479e1b0983648d0db0808f5856d63f" :answer/id #uuid "2f66c3ad-4b11-5cfb-85dc-f891d1bff6eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection/e70d9c96125ed943a2a4bcee52f18650c8984e4ea589517a42ddb08385c54e77" :answer/id #uuid "75e1e9b8-36d8-5956-964d-15ff2864c4c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+8n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ee74ced-73c3-540e-b4ee-6116255b1f85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117618/selection/64f4bdd26daf769cdf1888fb84a5697a3bec3a99a1ded94774a821635dd157ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-117618/selection/64f4bdd26daf769cdf1888fb84a5697a3bec3a99a1ded94774a821635dd157ba" "q-117618/selection/bf9716302ce7c9f50805073e08d4170912d0e97c55ba14de9b2570374d0b53cb" "q-117618/selection/4b55faefad2d0bf5e9b0f1e409536c4e172f1ff4106c57bacd0941fab6fd652d" "q-117618/selection/edcfd6d065adde0faa5b121e19e939fbfc479e1b0983648d0db0808f5856d63f" "q-117618/selection/e70d9c96125ed943a2a4bcee52f18650c8984e4ea589517a42ddb08385c54e77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117618" :question/id #uuid "706da7d1-15ea-5bec-aa0a-30b2bfa962bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-117618" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=(2n+1)\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =(2n+1)\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =2n\\pi +\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+8n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=\\frac{8\\pi }{3}+8n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117618/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e981a4-ba75-5db2-81ab-b321953cc225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection/4aea5d4e617d374d1c728fcfce84c0a0c8d87c0b7a142fe8a7844ef56ddaf5ea" :answer/id #uuid "4c4d58d6-8bc8-507b-8f0e-9e56ac9b6965" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pi +2\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection/a86b7586fc314cc814294438566a7d4f41d1d0970963912b55d20f6db1384704" :answer/id #uuid "a0873e2d-bd14-5ea0-a642-453e7fc8146f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pi +3\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection/1056766aa68ff14d3899a5652cbfe529232278c6a2341614ae289c4cbde2e9d6" :answer/id #uuid "d6b6acd2-2339-534f-99e3-35a78c9e6a3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection/9d2adc502888aefcacb68be62f95f95b5eb569ddf6826fba608a5e0c0079144d" :answer/id #uuid "bf92c4b0-60ec-57c4-a752-cea1cf7e0fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{15\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection/eaea100b1d5392fddba74a983edc8ca62e747971257b9658f98cd21e2550e312" :answer/id #uuid "7abc315a-df85-5808-a5e3-431f90ce1561" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+3\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "127d56b5-3f60-57ec-9a4d-a8eb7e8d5cd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81536/selection/9d2adc502888aefcacb68be62f95f95b5eb569ddf6826fba608a5e0c0079144d" :answer-field/choices ["q-81536/selection/4aea5d4e617d374d1c728fcfce84c0a0c8d87c0b7a142fe8a7844ef56ddaf5ea" "q-81536/selection/a86b7586fc314cc814294438566a7d4f41d1d0970963912b55d20f6db1384704" "q-81536/selection/1056766aa68ff14d3899a5652cbfe529232278c6a2341614ae289c4cbde2e9d6" "q-81536/selection/9d2adc502888aefcacb68be62f95f95b5eb569ddf6826fba608a5e0c0079144d" "q-81536/selection/eaea100b1d5392fddba74a983edc8ca62e747971257b9658f98cd21e2550e312"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81536" :question/id #uuid "82548378-f478-5059-a129-9b54510feafc" :question/math-academy-id "q-81536" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=(2n+1)\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =(2n+1)\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\pi +2\\pi n \\\\ \\frac{x}{3} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}+2\\pi n \\\\ x & =\\frac{15\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=\\frac{15\\pi }{4}+6\\pi n,$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81536/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e981a4-ba75-5db2-81ab-b321953cc225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81536"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection/c296eedf3acc0835cd67b813578e552998dee75276b092b97d3e8c5d4000166f" :answer/id #uuid "d21faab5-3130-5cb4-b16e-6e6bcf2ee7bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}+10\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection/21cf27a127c7e79739498889d7dc08bb01d3d5e677ab486dbce87052ad2e4a01" :answer/id #uuid "210c29e7-c648-55ef-9f38-03a75517eaf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{2\\pi n}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection/076ca44206d7583685fad780e39fedbffb33c693103ba0d1b3015acee7163556" :answer/id #uuid "28273583-3018-5c52-aa16-c6c033fee2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=10\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection/40a6fccaa29e1e9c7fff85f21c12cabd09f7d8566ba847ab3f86de9259bcb377" :answer/id #uuid "700ac781-6d79-546e-b2ec-d055de5f4067" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection/4d73ef4898ce46d74bdd00f505b59cd2d16bc51fd55ef16a7a108e39d68c2a84" :answer/id #uuid "63f4e240-2736-5e72-91e8-00eafcb340ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5\\pi (2n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "994895cb-6e83-51cf-8c5d-1995675dbac0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81534/selection/4d73ef4898ce46d74bdd00f505b59cd2d16bc51fd55ef16a7a108e39d68c2a84" :answer-field/choices ["q-81534/selection/c296eedf3acc0835cd67b813578e552998dee75276b092b97d3e8c5d4000166f" "q-81534/selection/21cf27a127c7e79739498889d7dc08bb01d3d5e677ab486dbce87052ad2e4a01" "q-81534/selection/076ca44206d7583685fad780e39fedbffb33c693103ba0d1b3015acee7163556" "q-81534/selection/40a6fccaa29e1e9c7fff85f21c12cabd09f7d8566ba847ab3f86de9259bcb377" "q-81534/selection/4d73ef4898ce46d74bdd00f505b59cd2d16bc51fd55ef16a7a108e39d68c2a84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81534" :question/id #uuid "a6ff2b03-e698-532e-8606-026d7ada5574" :question/math-academy-id "q-81534" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{5}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x}{5}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=(2n+1)\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =(2n+1)\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =(2n+1)\\pi  \\\\ x & =5\\pi (2n+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=5\\pi (2n+1),$ where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81534/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e981a4-ba75-5db2-81ab-b321953cc225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81534"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection/ec7f4de4df3bde9fb3f52ac88710264950e27e31b4d87aeb8ac8f1a15cf9bd09" :answer/id #uuid "b43e049b-4777-54f2-9169-76d68ae937df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection/aac173d1da5ebf0b52fae27fd69868be7f7f198ab920bfed967c75672b89ad2d" :answer/id #uuid "9a3f643e-5581-55fe-ba4e-0a55e0c5298a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection/578ccf6a88e0d6a80ddaa340894846916404738ebdb07a224eb38b306f5297f4" :answer/id #uuid "ed57c608-9afa-5aa9-bf7f-5bffbbc0afd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{10}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection/30c31b46904eca94c7e37d6343f9066a3acebe4a65eb69f9cc0e69d53cb91393" :answer/id #uuid "6c8270af-f37d-5b55-9606-ac2b39fc71ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{n\\pi }{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection/ab26413f81089e157d0448d67f78ead61aba1659ea40aa42665b796504e8a61e" :answer/id #uuid "472e6098-3721-5152-ae91-c4099f47aee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{10}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "428403ad-1ff6-5fcb-8a18-87e2a3d32520" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-117609/selection/ec7f4de4df3bde9fb3f52ac88710264950e27e31b4d87aeb8ac8f1a15cf9bd09" :answer-field/choices ["q-117609/selection/ec7f4de4df3bde9fb3f52ac88710264950e27e31b4d87aeb8ac8f1a15cf9bd09" "q-117609/selection/aac173d1da5ebf0b52fae27fd69868be7f7f198ab920bfed967c75672b89ad2d" "q-117609/selection/578ccf6a88e0d6a80ddaa340894846916404738ebdb07a224eb38b306f5297f4" "q-117609/selection/30c31b46904eca94c7e37d6343f9066a3acebe4a65eb69f9cc0e69d53cb91393" "q-117609/selection/ab26413f81089e157d0448d67f78ead61aba1659ea40aa42665b796504e8a61e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-117609" :question/id #uuid "6b7e329d-52d4-572d-bcbe-003c4b6ced95" :question/math-academy-id "q-117609" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 5x+\\frac{\\pi }{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ 5x & =-\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{5}+\\frac{2n\\pi }{5},$ where $n$ is any integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-117609/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e981a4-ba75-5db2-81ab-b321953cc225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-117609"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection/3799c569c9f0737fe0571b70d42db201c88baa97b629670c7422e26ac5865926" :answer/id #uuid "df91abe3-c316-5ef3-acd7-76976ebcbdc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection/04d1d829e52fecb475c91d3080b0d0624e939a009ef646668b831dcb8813731a" :answer/id #uuid "a5dc07c2-4c3d-5a25-a9ce-7abe26f8dbc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pi +n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection/bd8f94732e39109da911aef42e48f68154c3e1c21032c732f57787479a2ddc29" :answer/id #uuid "8b4316e3-4c85-5fac-8224-19831977273f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pi +4n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection/1dd641d746380fa3b2043390af4eb0ec391097ade750b94be7007c4eeb1a843a" :answer/id #uuid "17920a9d-9024-5301-ae57-e82e7dba4008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pi +3n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection/78a1b3190b455004e219fc990345e994138a02ea2104e438ab0d3971fdf0f898" :answer/id #uuid "de7e88b6-d134-5c25-aea2-0428f668b06c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2\\pi +5n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "047abde1-18c5-5000-9363-aee3a17d8216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65937/selection/3799c569c9f0737fe0571b70d42db201c88baa97b629670c7422e26ac5865926" :answer-field/choices ["q-65937/selection/3799c569c9f0737fe0571b70d42db201c88baa97b629670c7422e26ac5865926" "q-65937/selection/04d1d829e52fecb475c91d3080b0d0624e939a009ef646668b831dcb8813731a" "q-65937/selection/bd8f94732e39109da911aef42e48f68154c3e1c21032c732f57787479a2ddc29" "q-65937/selection/1dd641d746380fa3b2043390af4eb0ec391097ade750b94be7007c4eeb1a843a" "q-65937/selection/78a1b3190b455004e219fc990345e994138a02ea2104e438ab0d3971fdf0f898"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65937" :question/id #uuid "326f3c07-1bed-5ec8-b7b6-28fcd984ac05" :question/math-academy-id "q-65937" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x-3\\pi }{2}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer" :question/worked-solution "First, let's start by defining a new variable $X$ as\n\n$$\nX=\\frac{x-3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we need to calculate $X$-values at the minima of\n\n$$\nf(x)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡X.\n$$\n\nThe $X$-values at the minima are given by the following expression:\n\n$$\nX=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi \n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the $x$-values at the minima of our original function, we rewrite $X$ in terms of the original variable $x$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x-3\\pi }{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2\\pi +4n\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the values of $x$ that minimize $f(x)$ are given by $x=2\\pi +4n\\pi ,$  where $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-65937/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75e981a4-ba75-5db2-81ab-b321953cc225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
